---
---

<section id="best-time" class="section">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <!-- Section Header -->
    <div class="reveal mb-12 text-center">
      <span class="badge">Plan Your Visit</span>
      <h2 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-navy sm:text-4xl">
        Best Time to Visit
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <!-- Best Seasons -->
      <div class="reveal card p-8">
        <div class="mb-5 flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-gold-light/50">
          <svg class="h-6 w-6 text-gold" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 3v1m0 16v1m9-9h-1M4 12H3m15.364 6.364l-.707-.707M6.343 6.343l-.707-.707m12.728 0l-.707.707M6.343 17.657l-.707.707" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-navy">Dry Season (Nov — Apr)</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-stone leading-relaxed">
          The ideal window to visit. Expect clear blue skies, manageable temperatures,
          and the most vibrant photo conditions. December through February is peak
          season — plan ahead for accommodation in Laoag or Pagudpud.
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-sm text-stone">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <svg class="mt-0.5 h-4 w-4 flex-shrink-0 text-green" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" />
            </svg>
            Clear skies for dramatic turbine-against-ocean photos
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <svg class="mt-0.5 h-4 w-4 flex-shrink-0 text-green" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" />
            </svg>
            Perfect for combining with Pagudpud beaches and Kapurpurawan
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <!-- Time of Day + Duration -->
      <div class="reveal card p-8">
        <div class="mb-5 flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-sky-light/50">
          <svg class="h-6 w-6 text-ocean" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 8v4l3 3m6-3a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-navy">Time of Day</h3>
        <div class="mt-3 space-y-3 text-stone leading-relaxed">
          <div>
            <strong class="text-navy">Sunrise (5:30–7:00 AM)</strong>
            — The turbines silhouetted against the golden dawn over the West Philippine
            Sea. Fewer crowds, cooler temperatures, and the most dramatic light.
          </div>
          <div>
            <strong class="text-navy">Late Afternoon (3:00–5:30 PM)</strong>
            — Soft golden light for photography as the sun begins to dip behind the
            Ilocos mountains. Popular with tour groups.
          </div>
          <div>
            <strong class="text-navy">Midday</strong>
            — Harsh overhead light and stronger heat. If visiting, bring water,
            sunscreen, and a hat — shade is limited along the viewing area.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Suggested Duration -->
      <div class="reveal card p-8 lg:col-span-2">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-navy">Suggested Stay Duration</h3>
        <div class="mt-4 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
          <div class="rounded-xl bg-turbine/50 p-5 text-center">
            <div class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-ocean">30–45</div>
            <div class="mt-1 text-sm text-stone">Minutes (Quick Stop)</div>
            <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-stone/70">Photo ops at the viewing area. Enough if you're on a tight Ilocos day tour.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-xl bg-turbine/50 p-5 text-center">
            <div class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-ocean">1–2</div>
            <div class="mt-1 text-sm text-stone">Hours (Relaxed Visit)</div>
            <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-stone/70">Walk the shoreline, take photos from multiple angles, buy souvenirs and empanada.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-xl bg-turbine/50 p-5 text-center">
            <div class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-ocean">Half Day</div>
            <div class="mt-1 text-sm text-stone">(With Nearby Spots)</div>
            <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-stone/70">Combine with Kapurpurawan Rock Formation, Cape Bojeador Lighthouse, and Burgos Wind Farm.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Typhoon warning -->
        <div class="mt-6 flex items-start gap-3 rounded-xl border border-gold/30 bg-gold-light/10 p-4">
          <svg class="mt-0.5 h-5 w-5 flex-shrink-0 text-gold" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 9v2m0 4h.01m-6.938 4h13.856c1.54 0 2.502-1.667 1.732-2.5L13.732 4c-.77-.833-1.964-.833-2.732 0L4.082 16.5c-.77.833.192 2.5 1.732 2.5z" />
          </svg>
          <div>
            <strong class="text-sm text-navy">Rainy & Typhoon Season (Jun — Oct)</strong>
            <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-stone">
              Strong winds and heavy rain may limit visibility and access. Typhoons can
              affect Ilocos Norte — always check weather forecasts before traveling during
              these months.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
